From 277d5411da1799ab8e34a6a4e8ac4218abfa34cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:06:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Stop decoding an integer once it cannot be a uint32_t

lshpack_dec_dec_int's continuation loop is bounded by the buffer, not by
the encoding: it reads while the high bit is set and src < src_end. The
shift M grows by 7 each time, so the sixth continuation octet is added
with

    val = val + ((B & 0x7f) << M)

at M == 35, and B is a uint32_t. A shift wider than the type is
undefined (C17 6.5.7p3). LSHPACK_UINT32_ENC_SZ already names the limit -
six octets, the prefix and five continuations, the last shifted by 28 -
but it is only consulted when the BUFFER runs out, not when the encoding
does.

test/test_int.c reaches it with its own case:

    { .it_prefix_bits = 7,
      .it_encoded = { 0x7F, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF,
                      0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0xFF },
      .it_enc_sz = 11, .it_dec_retval = -2 },

    lshpack.c:1329:37: runtime error: shift exponent 35 is too large
                       for 32-bit type 'unsigned int'

The bound is checked before the octet is consumed, so an encoding of six
or more continuations returns -2 without shifting. That is the value the
post-loop check already produced for those inputs - M would be 42 or
more, and it accepts only M <= 28 or M == 35 - so no accepted encoding
changes. The 6-octet UINT32_MAX case in test_int still decodes.
---
 lshpack.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lshpack.c b/lshpack.c
index 7c7d4eb..d539dff 100644
--- a/lshpack.c
+++ b/lshpack.c
@@ -1326,6 +1326,17 @@ lshpack_dec_dec_int (const unsigned char **src_p, const unsigned char *src_end,
     {
         if (src < src_end)
         {
+            /* A uint32_t integer is at most LSHPACK_UINT32_ENC_SZ octets
+             * (RFC 7541 5.1): the prefix and five continuations, the last
+             * of which is shifted by 28.  Without this bound the loop
+             * keeps reading while the high bit is set, and the sixth
+             * continuation shifts by 35 - undefined for a 32-bit type.
+             * The check below rejects such an encoding anyway (M would be
+             * 42, which neither of its arms accepts), so this returns the
+             * same -2 it always did, before the shift instead of after.
+             */
+            if (src - orig_src >= LSHPACK_UINT32_ENC_SZ)
+                return -2;
             B = *src++;
             val = val + ((B & 0x7f) << M);
             M += 7;
